=== mls-3: L2: CTE MIN/MAX(CHAR) over 20000 redistributed groups, MIN/MAX again in the main join ===
idle level before the first execution: QUERY_MEMORY and TRANSACTION_MEMORY recorded on all 4 data nodes
reference run: 1 execution(s) via RDRS, every result identical to the reference
warm-up: 8 execution(s) via RDRS, 8 concurrent clients, every 200 response identical to the reference
first use: QUERY_MEMORY and TRANSACTION_MEMORY within the first-use allowance on all 4 data nodes
== Query ==
WITH st AS (
SELECT lg_cust AS k, MIN(lg_status) AS mn, MAX(lg_status) AS mx, COUNT(*) AS n
FROM lg_orders GROUP BY lg_cust)
SELECT c.lc_region, COUNT(*), SUM(st.n), MIN(st.mn), MAX(st.mx)
FROM lg_cust AS c JOIN st ON st.k = c.lc_id
GROUP BY c.lc_region;

Number of output lines, including header: 6

== Diff ==
==========




=== mls-4: L2: CTE MIN/MAX(VARCHAR) over 20000 groups, MIN/MAX again in the main join ===
idle level before the first execution: QUERY_MEMORY and TRANSACTION_MEMORY recorded on all 4 data nodes
reference run: 1 execution(s) via RDRS, every result identical to the reference
warm-up: 8 execution(s) via RDRS, 8 concurrent clients, every 200 response identical to the reference
first use: QUERY_MEMORY and TRANSACTION_MEMORY within the first-use allowance on all 4 data nodes
== Query ==
WITH seg AS (
SELECT lc_id AS k, MIN(lc_segment) AS mn, MAX(lc_segment) AS mx
FROM lg_cust GROUP BY lc_id)
SELECT c.lc_region, COUNT(*), MIN(seg.mn), MAX(seg.mx)
FROM lg_cust AS c JOIN seg ON seg.k = c.lc_id
GROUP BY c.lc_region;

